-- title:
--   Integrality of inertia-fixed positions in a p-adic annulus
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $p$ in the sense that $p$ is a non-unit of $A$, and let $F_0$ be an intermediate field between $\mathbb{Q}$ and the Laurent series field $\mathbb{Q}((q))$. Write $F = \overline{\mathbb{Q}}\cdot F_0$ for `laurentBaseChange`, the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the coefficientwise image of $F_0$; each $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ gives, via `arithmeticGalois`, the semilinear automorphism of $F$ acting on coefficients by $\sigma$, and so acts on elements of $F$ and on the places of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (a place being a proper valuation subring of $F$ containing $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose ring is a principal ideal ring). Let `An` be an annulus for $A$ in $F$: a set `An.dom` of places, a parameter $z =$ `An.param` $\in F$ and a modulus $\pi =$ `An.modulus` in the maximal ideal of $A$, subject to the annulus axioms — every $P \in$ `An.dom` is rational over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (the structure map to its residue field is surjective, so evaluation `P.evalAt` is defined by inverting it), $z$ lies in $P$, the value $P(z)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$, is nonzero, and $\pi \in P(z)\cdot\mathfrak{m}_A$; conversely every such value is attained by a unique place of the domain; $z - P(z)$ has order $1$ at each $P$; and the unit principle holds. Assume that $z$ is fixed by every $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ (the image in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ of the inertia subgroup inside the decomposition subgroup), and let $V \in$ `An.dom` be a place that is likewise fixed by every such $\sigma$. Then there is a natural number $d \ge 1$ with
--   $$v_A\bigl(V(z)\bigr) = v_A(p)^{\,d}, \qquad v_A(\pi) < v_A(p)^{\,d},$$
--   where $v_A$ is the multiplicatively written valuation attached to $A$, so that the second condition says that $\pi$ is strictly more divisible than $p^{d}$.
--
--   The result expresses that the position of an inertia-fixed point in a $p$-adic annulus with inertia-fixed parameter is integral: its valuation is an exact power of $v_A(p)$, bounded by the thickness of the annulus. It is what allows a depth to be attached to an inertia-fixed place lying over a node of the special fibre of a semistable modular curve, and is used in [`ModularCurve.JHPlaceSpecialization.exists_depth_forall_annulusDepthLaw`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JHPlaceSpecialization.exists_depth_forall_annulusDepthLaw).
